  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM EDT Sat May 30 2026\n\nHigh pressure to the north will help to reinforce a dry and stable \ncolumn within low level easterly flow through midweek. A well \nadvertised omega block will help lock this feature in place with low \nhumidity, ample sunshine and seasonable temperatures. \n\nThe blocking pattern breaks down mid-late week with the upstream \nupper ridge folding into the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley. Return \nflow with the surface high shifting southeast will result in a \nwarming trend with highs well into the 80s by Thursday and Friday. \nChances for showers/storms will also make an appearance later Friday \ninto Saturday as a trough axis tracks east into an increasingly \nhumid air mass.",
